details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. Two shallow, matte ceramic bowls are positioned on a rustic, aged oak tabletop, one sharp in the foreground and one slightly blurred behind it. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring every component is clearly visible. Each bowl is filled with a vibrant base of fluffy, off-white cooked quinoa, earthy black beans, bright yellow diced mango, and crisp crimson red bell pepper, all lightly tossed in an olive oil and lime dressing. Several perfectly pink, opaque, seared shrimp with subtle charred edges are arranged neatly on top of the quinoa, next to the mango and beans so they remain distinct. The bowls are garnished with freshly chopped green scallions and fragrant cilantro leaves. Soft natural light from a window on the left creates subtle highlights on the mango and the moist sheen of the lime-dressed quinoa. A rumpled linen napkin rests casually beside the bowls, with a few stray cilantro leaves and a small pinch of scattered red pepper flakes on the wooden surface. A wooden spoon lies beside the front bowl, looking as if just used. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures an authentic, lived-in kitchen atmosphere. Includes slight natural imperfections like an asymmetric garnish and a tiny sauce drip on a bowl rim. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no hands, no text. The image is indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
}
